{"title":"2020 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 8","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(bashing)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (bashing)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Solution_8\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 8</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Solution_9\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 9</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Solution_10_(very_similar_to_solution_7)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 10 (very similar to solution 7)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Solution_11\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 11</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">15</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-16\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">16</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/4/6546d929f5a85740556d362a0491e8e13a4b9948.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1+2+3-4+5+6+7-8+\\cdots+197+198+199-200?\\]\" width=\"475\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/e/2be28e75d7676e3ee1218fe9fb5c872d4ff30ae4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 9,800 \\qquad \\textbf{(B) } 9,900 \\qquad \\textbf{(C) } 10,000 \\qquad \\textbf{(D) } 10,100 \\qquad \\textbf{(E) } 10,200$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"556\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Looking at the numbers, you see that every set of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> positive numbers and 1 negative number. Calculating the sum of the first couple sets gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/8/eb809fb6b20557c60b5d1071d19f7ff090f733f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2+10+18...+394$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"154\" height=\"14\" />. Clearly, this pattern is an arithmetic sequence. By using the formula we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/0/a80b897db8d877c29b4d5c8b1ce2fbf958ad9e5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2+394}{2}\\cdot 50=\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }9900}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"202\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>-ViratKohli2018\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Split the even numbers and the odd numbers apart. If we group every 2 even numbers together and add them, we get a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/9/079545f27a4cfd4e9e510f51850e3c914f424e11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50\\cdot (-2)=-100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"133\" height=\"18\" />. Summing the odd numbers is equivalent to summing the first 100 odd numbers, which is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/3/d53b48e06adbe9aba421a4d1dd527a4a886821b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100^2=10000$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"103\" height=\"15\" />. Adding these two, we obtain the answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/b/54bc4cd2f5f14f8e1683790b4eefe605c413bd15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }9900}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"83\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28bashing.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(bashing)\">Solution 3 (bashing)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (bashing)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can break this entire sum down into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> integer bits, in which the sum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/c/2ec701493fa72dda5d6747fe14f30e7b1c2fb6c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is the first integer in this bit. We can find that the first sum of every sequence is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/3/1f32849858c8d26bb33d6687c58a215f959937ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4x-3$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"50\" height=\"13\" />, which we plug in for the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/906734e2f1010e9a171ffee8050cbc0649cea37c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> bits in the entire sequence is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/d/3fde2607d9d114306b877bd46fca4ee30115a0d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+2+3+\\cdots+50=1275$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"215\" height=\"14\" />, so then we can plug it into the first term of every sequence equation we got above <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/e/2be3bb8935aa349ff2ea8178fb090468d3f11b88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4(1275)-3(50)=4950$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"183\" height=\"18\" />, and so the sum of every bit is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/c/2ec701493fa72dda5d6747fe14f30e7b1c2fb6c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" />, and we only found the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, the sum of the sequence is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/1/9511ad279255adb8b031c818cf8d3dbabeb65de1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4950\\cdot2=\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) } 9900}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"165\" height=\"28\" />.-middletonkids\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Another solution involves adding everything and subtracting out what is not needed.  The first step involves solving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/d/79d8b359aa0f0a8cc5bf88a8c913dfe3063b3814.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+2+3+4+5+6+7+8+\\cdots+197+198+199+200$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"469\" height=\"14\" />.  To do this, we can simply multiply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/3/8f37626d49b4082c9102bf930bca51277ff2eb43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$200$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/3/1038785e77cdf7734f6ee2f8fed6de2ab19acc15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$201$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> and divide by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to get us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/2/b22797b364123e0bb3dfd91ec3d16693019c1c23.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20100$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"44\" height=\"13\" />.  The next step involves subtracting out the numbers with minus signs.  We actually have to do this twice, because we need to take out the numbers we weren’t supposed to add and then subtract them from the problem.  Then, we can see that from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/3/8f37626d49b4082c9102bf930bca51277ff2eb43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$200$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />, incrementing by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/906734e2f1010e9a171ffee8050cbc0649cea37c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> numbers that we have to subtract.  To do this we can do <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/906734e2f1010e9a171ffee8050cbc0649cea37c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> times <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/1/6e1fd7cb028e27b8648efbfb002f3e6d4fcb33a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$51$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and then we can multiply by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, because we are counting by fours, not ones.  Our answer will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/4/8142a8ba1835e03caa441684ab3b9592195994a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5100$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" />, but remember, we have to do this twice.  Once we do that, we will get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/6/096148aea77f6c179c97cd08014e82d13d240b7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10200$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"44\" height=\"13\" />.  Finally, we just have to do <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/6/e5646cce23b81c19b59a270ff8d61530ed4257f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20100-10200$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"112\" height=\"13\" />, and our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/b/54bc4cd2f5f14f8e1683790b4eefe605c413bd15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }9900}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"83\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>— <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/e/13e2ddb6215e139abe1deea1ccbbd4758f64ded9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{Phineas}1500$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"92\" height=\"13\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In this solution, we group every 4 terms. Our groups should be: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/1/1913a604de990d1d9b72c40405ab3a19ee9c69cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + 2 + 3 - 4 = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"136\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/4/6d4c3ae5f052491b424c60c2ae60e8c94500db35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 + 6 + 7 - 8 = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"145\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/b/a3b1346b74c2ebb70005156ddb5f9c3a0ba2c456.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9 + 10 + 11 - 12 = 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"175\" height=\"15\" />, ... <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/4/fc489ec3ad62b23bf7645631ba9f60f02b374c06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$197 + 198 + 199 - 200 = 394$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"227\" height=\"14\" />. We add them together to get this expression: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/5/cd50f8861ef98fc2ce9f4b2eb5437b42380d3aa6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 + 10 + 18 + ... + 394$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"176\" height=\"14\" />. This can be rewritten as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/c/09c6bf7e36116932a06580f86eadba716d255633.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8 * (0 + 1 + 2 + ... + 49) + 100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"238\" height=\"18\" />. We add this to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/b/54bc4cd2f5f14f8e1683790b4eefe605c413bd15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }9900}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"83\" height=\"28\" />.    ~Baolan\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6\">Solution 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can split up this long sum into groups of four integers. Finding the first few sums, we have that  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/1/1913a604de990d1d9b72c40405ab3a19ee9c69cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + 2 + 3 - 4 = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"136\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/4/6d4c3ae5f052491b424c60c2ae60e8c94500db35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 + 6 + 7 - 8 = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"145\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/b/a3b1346b74c2ebb70005156ddb5f9c3a0ba2c456.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9 + 10 + 11 - 12 = 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"175\" height=\"15\" />. Notice that this is an increasing arithmetic sequence, with a common difference of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. We can find the sum of the arithmetic sequence by finding the average of the first and last terms, and then multiplying by the number of terms in the sequence. The first term is  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/b/cbb668da95c785af525912981346f83437c43f7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + 2 + 3 - 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"103\" height=\"14\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, the last term is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/6/606101a2009210ce2eee5bbc5d61098fc3791108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$197 + 198 + 199 - 200$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"175\" height=\"14\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/0/1b05695bcf42128cea94f5178b0453bd64f3ffe7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$394$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" />, and there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/1/751e19ef6a5b5fd08b0d781e46575c10c0958575.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$200\\div 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/906734e2f1010e9a171ffee8050cbc0649cea37c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> terms. So, we have that the sum of the sequence is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/c/7fccd58df3a48e914d4b684ebfe041a4b334d507.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{(394+2)\\cdot 50}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"106\" height=\"38\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/b/54bc4cd2f5f14f8e1683790b4eefe605c413bd15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }9900}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"83\" height=\"28\" />. ~Arctic_Bunny\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_7\">Solution 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that the original expression is equal to\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/d/86dd65b489f6925451f5ce387f4f935a9b63df52.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(1+2+3+\\dots+199+200)-2(4(1+2+3+\\dots+49+50)).\\]\" width=\"476\" height=\"18\" />\nSince the sum of the first <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> positive integers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/f/64f8070867b03b0dc224db7e741135e07f4502c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{n(n+1)}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"69\" height=\"38\" />, this is equal to\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/1/e3117279c38e869ba84992251692cc9967c82232.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{200(201)}{2}-2\\left(4\\left(\\frac{50(51)}{2}\\right)\\right),\\]\" width=\"231\" height=\"43\" />\nwhich can be simplified as\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/8/018baf28724fdf48bcc0b2356de698df323c0537.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[20100-4(50)(51)=20100-10200.\\]\" width=\"281\" height=\"18\" />\nDoing the subtraction yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/b/54bc4cd2f5f14f8e1683790b4eefe605c413bd15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }9900}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"83\" height=\"28\" />. -BorealBear\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_8\">Solution 8</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 8\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can split the sum into 4 groups so that the terms in these groups have the same common difference of 4\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/1/fe1d3f08a78cc9b2ccda6bfaff86bb8f04738a00.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1+5+9+...+197)+(2+6+10+...+198)+(3+7+11+...+199)-(4+8+12+...+200)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"787\" height=\"20\" />.\nThen, we can use the sum formula. It's equal to\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/d/19dc42ef93eb9e01e332095e2099c0d01ffa1e0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{50\\cdot(1+197)}{2} + \\frac{50\\cdot(2+198)}{2} + \\frac{50\\cdot(3+199)}{2} - \\frac{50\\cdot(4+200)}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"501\" height=\"40\" />.\nThis can also be expressed as\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/9/b89404c699c44ba83e44a221836818d78f853d8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(25\\cdot198) + (25\\cdot200) + (25\\cdot202) - (25\\cdot204)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"359\" height=\"20\" />.\nAnd it is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/8/4382e6a8946b3e32d99a8cc33364d537266441a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25\\cdot(198+200+202-204) = 25\\cdot396 = 9900$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"366\" height=\"20\" />.\nTherefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/b/54bc4cd2f5f14f8e1683790b4eefe605c413bd15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }9900}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"83\" height=\"28\" />. ~kurbanlik_21\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_9\">Solution 9</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 9\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can split the answer into trios of sums and a difference:\n(1+2+3) + (5+6+7) + (9+10+11) ... + (197+198+199) - (4+8+12+ ... + 200).\nWe note that each of our trios are consecutive integers so replace them by their average - e.g., 5+6+7 = 3*6.\n</p><p>We have 3 (2+6+10+ ... +198) - 4 (1+2+3+ ... + 50) = 3A - 4B.\nHow we can use a \"rainbow\" method for A to add 2+198 = 6+194 = .... How many terms do we have?\n2, 6, 10, ..., 198 has the same number of terms as the sequence\n0, 4, 8, ..., 198-2 = 196, which has the same number of terms as the sequence\n0, 1, 2, ..., 196/4 = 49\nSo there are 50 terms, which means 50/2 = 25 pairs of 200. A is 25*200\nB is just 50*51/2 = 25*51\n</p><p>So we have 3(25*200) - 4(25*51) = 100(150-51) = 9900\n~Dilip\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_10_.28very_similar_to_solution_7.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_10_(very_similar_to_solution_7)\">Solution 10 (very similar to solution 7)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 10 (very similar to solution 7)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can treat the negative numbers separately than the rest of the sequence.\n</p><p>The negative numbers are as follows: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/7/3273b06dbf07130bce9d2af093811210b1765c9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-4, -8, -12,... -200$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"170\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>Summing all of the negative numbers up <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/3/9832ea7977e7fbf78164d374d1b4d1159bd45ace.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[-51*(25*4)]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"120\" height=\"20\" /> (first dividing the negative sequence by 4, using Gauss to add all of the numbers up, then re-multiplying by 4), we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/4/5346586a389aaabcf3217cf00234c9b550c0877a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-5100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Now, we can add up the original sequence as if there were no negative numbers (so converting all negatives into positives), to which we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/2/b22797b364123e0bb3dfd91ec3d16693019c1c23.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20100$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"44\" height=\"13\" /> by having <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/1/fe1fea2579018cb3c7d4daa2035db4e61068c95f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$201*100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>We then subtract <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/4/8142a8ba1835e03caa441684ab3b9592195994a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5100$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/2/b22797b364123e0bb3dfd91ec3d16693019c1c23.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20100$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"44\" height=\"13\" /> twice (the first time to make all of the negative numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> in the sequence, second time to obtain the answer).\n</p><p>And we obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/b/54bc4cd2f5f14f8e1683790b4eefe605c413bd15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }9900}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"83\" height=\"28\" />. ~martianrunner\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_11\">Solution 11</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 11\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/d/e1dc005b5b676f6df1db897c48890fd2bc8f6875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1 + 2 + 3 + 4 + \\cdots + 199 + 200) - 8(1 + 2 + 3 + \\cdots + 49 + 50) = 100 \\cdot 201 - 8 \\cdot 25 \\cdot 51 = 100(201 - 102) = 100(99) = \\boxed{9900}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"987\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~ilikemath247365\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1\">Video Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Education, The Study of Everything\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/xoIWkRr0BOo\">https://youtu.be/xoIWkRr0BOo</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2\">Video Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/JEjib74EmiY\">https://youtu.be/JEjib74EmiY</a>\n</p><p>~IceMatrix\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_3\">Video Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=15\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/8osKFz1CMSc\">https://youtu.be/8osKFz1CMSc</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=16\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A\" title=\"2020 AMC 10A\">2020 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2020 AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2020 AMC 10A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2020 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2020 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2020 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2020 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2020 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2020 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2020 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2020 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2020 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2020 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2020 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2020 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2020 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2020 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2020 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2020 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2020 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2020 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2020 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2020 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2020 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2020 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2020 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2020 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2020 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2020 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_10_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 10 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 10 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017034433\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.056 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.077 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 519/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2320/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 154/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 14517/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   16.718      1 -total\n 56.35%    9.421      1 Template:AMC10_box\n 42.91%    7.174      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:18095:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017034433 and revision id 291418. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}